regime‑specific parameters

Cipher Module:An XOR‑based cipher operates on message payloads using (K(t)), producing hex‑encoded encrypted outputs.

Cryptographic State Provenance Spine:A structured record of:

Hamiltonian parameters

initial conditions

divergence metrics

key evolution history

This spine ties each encrypted stream to a specific physical/simulation regime.

Encrypted Simulation Stream:Continuous output combining:

simulation data

cryptographic transformation

provenance metadata

5. Mathematical Framework

5.1 Hamiltonian Gradients

[ \nabla H = \left( \frac{\partial H}{\partial q_{bio}}, \frac{\partial H}{\partial p_{bio}}, \frac{\partial H}{\partial q_{astro}}, \frac{\partial H}{\partial p_{astro}} \right) ]

5.2 Divergence Sampling

Chaotic trajectories are sampled at discrete time steps (\Delta t):

[ {x(t_0), x(t_1), \dots, x(t_n)} ]

These samples form entropy pools used in key derivation.

5.3 Key Mapping

A mapping function:

[ K(t_i) = g(x(t_i), \lambda(t_i)) ]

converts sampled states and divergence metrics into cryptographic key material.

